#!/bin/bash
cat <<'TXT'
 Xiaomi Mi 5 - Ubuntu: easy commands
 ------------------------------------------------------------
 menu              menu with everything below (arrows + Enter)
 wifi              connect to WiFi (pick from a list)
 wifi status       am I online? what is my IP?
 wifi fix          WiFi stopped working -> reset it
 wifi hotspot      phone becomes a hotspot: join it, ssh ubuntu@10.42.0.1
 status            battery, WiFi, temperature, ...
 install-claude    install / update Claude Code
 claude            start Claude Code   (claude-tmux: survives disconnects)
 install-pi        install pi agent + DeepSeek key
 pi                start pi            (pi-tmux: survives disconnects)
 bright 40         screen brightness in %
 screen-timeout 60 screen off after 60 s idle (0 = never)
 update            update Ubuntu (apt)
 sudo reboot       restart          sudo poweroff   shut down
 ------------------------------------------------------------
 Keys: Power = screen on/off (hold 3 s = power off)
       Volume up/down = arrow up/down, Home button = Enter
 USB cable to a PC: ssh ubuntu@172.16.42.1
 No WiFi for ~10 min: the phone starts hotspot "Mi5-Ubuntu"
   by itself (password: wifi status, or /etc/default/gemini)
TXT
